Private copied zero-test selection — 2026-10-19

Machine selection replaces a private copy followed by a final compare with
zero and an equal/not-equal branch with CBZ/CBNZ on the source value. Both
the copied value and flags must have one definition and one use. W/W, W/X
and X/X copies preserve the zero test; X/W narrowing is excluded. Targets,
edge arguments and execution obligations do not change. This is ordinary
machine selection, not a certified EqSat rewrite or guard removal.

Unchanged sources and kernel argv, 100000 calls per case:
Symbol           Before/call After/call GCC14/call Before bytes After bytes
theta                    171        171         94          728         728
pte_offset_map            52         46         23          276         252
folio_state               32         32          9          152         152
Three container and three TCG executions agree on the retained checksums,
with no dropped or irregular blocks. GCC counts are retained, not rerun.
The final gate-built compiler reproduces all three measured assemblies byte
for byte. The array and record meet their stated 2x GCC instruction limits.
Library-only executed-path refusals remain non-PASS. The projected kernel
argv still discloses unsupported -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks and
-fno-common; this is not a claim of complete Kbuild option parity.

Tests cover both targets, W/X transport, high-bit boundaries, narrowing,
shared values, outgoing arguments, signed comparisons and changed branches.
The real proof-required path checks final assembly; wrong branch polarity
or operands are rejected at lowering. The Lean zero-test lemma is width
parameterized and adds no axiom. Full acceptance: 458 Rust suites, 3473
passed, zero failed, eight ignored, Clippy and formatting pass. All six Lean
steps pass: 88434 vectors, 62 rule theorems, 36 analysis rows, 576 enumerated
instances and 11 named expectations. The 975 whole-environment axioms are
not a TCB count. The separate six-group correspondence campaign was not
rerun. The shared tree is dirty, so this is not clean release acceptance.

